# centralize_events_lobby_name_change_udp — client 1 (slot 0).
# DS runs with the lobby state machine live. The headless's
# cmd-stdin pump falls back to a per-iteration counter while
# serverTick is still 0, so these lobby ops fire on wall-clock
# cadence (~1ms per pump tick).
#
# Sequencing mirrors centralize_events_lobby_smoke_udp: both
# clients set team early, the rename fires in lobby phase well
# before either client readies, and c1 readies LAST so its
# ready is the trigger that tips serverSimLobbyCheckAllReady
# over — not c1 readying alone before c2 has joined.
#
# The rename is the gate target: today the server filters out
# the renamer when broadcasting PACKET_NAME_CHANGE
# (transport_udp_server.c renamer-exclusion check), so c1's
# golden will NOT contain a CTRL_PLAYER_NAME entry for its own
# rename — but it WILL contain one for c2's rename below.
{"tick": 100,  "op": "set_team",    "slot": 0, "team": 1}
{"tick": 500,  "op": "name_change", "slot": 0, "name": "Renamed1"}
{"tick": 4000, "op": "set_ready",   "slot": 0, "ready": true}
